{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Scope Correction\nThis ticket originally tracked a loose-object ENOENT/write-tree failure. When Gerrit 1827 later failed with a batched-empty / narrow-success signature, the ticket was reopened under the assumption that it was the same failure class. Investigation refuted that assumption: deleting the previously implicated loose blob left both broad and narrow history walks healthy. The unresolved ENOENT symptom is preserved separately in previous-quelled-nutria, linked discovered_from this ticket and blocked on recurrence evidence. Historical comments below remain the audit trail; the current scope is only the distinct Gerrit 1827 recurrence.\n\n## Problem\nIn Gerrit 1827 run 31961655783, tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py called build_ticket_position_commit_map once and required a complete map. That optimization helper explicitly fails closed to an empty map on any Git nonzero result, empty output, or process exception; production callers then preserve attribution with per-event fallback. The fixture equivalence assertion incorrectly treated the optimization boundary as guaranteed to succeed on its first environmental attempt. The observed sequence was an empty batched result followed immediately by a successful narrow read in the unchanged repository.\n\n## Approach\n- Prove the recurrence boundary with the real temporary Git topology and first-attempt injections for rc 128 with empty output, rc 0 with empty output, and BlockingIOError(EAGAIN).\n- Add fixture-only bounded recovery that repeats the exact batched resolver call, returns only a complete map, and stops after five attempts with existing object-store diagnostics.\n- Route both direct equivalence assertions and the optimization-count assertion through the same fixture helper.\n- Keep src/rebar fail-closed and per-event fallback behavior unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The prior loose-object ENOENT class is refuted for this recurrence: deleting the implicated blob leaves both broad and narrow history reads successful; the residual ENOENT work is tracked in previous-quelled-nutria.\n- [x] First-attempt rc 128/empty, rc 0/empty, and BlockingIOError(EAGAIN) injections each reproduce the observed empty-batched then successful-identical-replay sequence against the real fixture repository.\n- [x] Fixture-only recovery makes at most five exact batched attempts, returns on the first complete map, and raises persistent diagnostics containing fsck and count-objects evidence; no src/rebar behavior changes.\n- [x] Both fixture equivalence assertions and the optimization-count assertion use the recovery seam without weakening exact position-to-commit expectations.\n- [x] Held-out TDD evidence is recorded: four behavioral cases were RED before the repair, GREEN afterward, and returned to RED under the exact omitted-recovery mutation; the in-file optimization sibling was independently RED then GREEN.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Focused tests (12 passed), adjacent suites (27 passed), lint, typecheck, and the full local suite (13,522 passed, 60 skipped, 289 deselected) are green; Gerrit 1828 earned LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with zero unresolved comments, merged as commit 29448f61c095c4f63afb9291ae156a4e0163d843, and CI run 31967631562 completed with 17 green jobs including Ubuntu/Python 3.11.\n  provenance: environment=local worktree and Gerrit CI; principal=RebarBotNava and rebar CI bot; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — commands, votes, merge state, and CI run were observed directly and recorded in the final repair comment.","title":"Verified-matrix authorship fixture: transient batched Git read returns empty before narrow fallback succeeds"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786911189972136001,"uuid":"61707f1f-df1b-4f0d-a849-5917d7934b4a"}